course: dictionary
lesson: 9543
title: Stonefish: hidden and venomous
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A stonefish is a fish that is very hard to spot. The sentence «The stonefish looks exactly like a lumpy stone» gives you the clue: it hides on the seabed by looking like a rock or a lump of coral. Animals that hide by blending in are using camouflage.
explain: Now look at «has venomous spines on its back that can sting a person who treads on it». Venomous means able to put poison into a body through a bite or a sting. Spines are sharp points, and treads on means steps on, so a stonefish is dangerous to step on.
explain: Use the context to check your meaning. Put «venomous» into the sentence: «spines that can put poison into a person who steps on them». Does it still make sense? Yes, so you have understood it correctly.
fact: A stonefish is a fish of warm, shallow seas, such as parts of the Indian and Pacific Oceans, including northern Australia.
fact: Stonefish look like rocks or lumps of coral, so they can hide on the seabed.
fact: «Venomous» means able to put poison into a body through a bite or sting.
fact: The stonefish is one of the most venomous fish in the world.
fact: In Australia, beach signs tell swimmers to wear «reef shoes» to protect their feet.
exercise: «The stonefish looks exactly like a lumpy stone.» What does the stonefish look like? | A bright blue bird | *A lumpy stone or a lump of coral | A long, thin snake
exercise: «Has venomous spines on its back.» What does venomous mean? | Shiny and smooth | Fast through the water | Very tasty to eat | *Able to put poison into you through a sting
exercise: Where does the stonefish live? | Cold, deep lakes in the mountains | Frozen seas near the poles | Dry deserts far from water | *Warm, shallow seas, including northern Australia
test: Why do Australian beach signs tell swimmers to wear «reef shoes»? | To make them swim faster | To keep their feet warm in cold water | *To protect their feet from stonefish spines | To help them float
test: «A person who treads on it» — what does treads on mean? | Looks at | *Steps on | Pulls away from | Swims past
exam: Why is the stonefish dangerous to step on? | *It has venomous spines that can sting, and it hides looking like a rock | It is very big and heavy | It makes loud noises in the water | It bites through shoes
